    "result_text": "All tests pass (BUILD SUCCESS). The full suite consists of the two `AcceptanceTest` cases (the other test files are the abstract `AcceptanceBase` and the `AuditLogCapture` helper), and both are green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` field, derived from `city` using the fixed city-to-region table, on the owner API response.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `locality` string property to the `Owner` response schema (alongside the other derived fields like `displayName`, `membershipTier`), so the OpenAPI generator produces `OwnerDto.locality`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` for `locality` computed inline in the `toOwnerDto` expression: `Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`, else `UNKNOWN`. This mirrors the existing inline-expression style used for `membershipTier`/`displayName`, and \u2014 being derived at mapping time from the current `city` \u2014 stays correct across updates.\n\n**A subtlety worth noting:** my first attempt used a `default String locality(String city)` helper method on the mapper. That silently broke *owner creation* (400s), because MapStruct treats any `String \u2192 String` method in the mapper as a candidate conversion and auto-applied it to every string field during the request-side `toOwner` mapping \u2014 corrupting `city`/`telephone`. I diagnosed this by confirming create returned 201 at baseline, then switched to an inline expression (adds no reusable mapping method), which resolves it cleanly.",
